zig0.17 (0.17.0~us1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build from upstream source instead of repacking upstream's binaries,
    following the layout of Ubuntu's zig0.16 packaging:
    - Rename the source package to zig0.17, and split the binary package
      into zig0.17 (compiler, /usr/bin/zig0.17) and zig0.17-dev (standard
      library, docs).
    - Build with CMake against the system LLVM/Clang/LLD 22.
    - Replace the vendored Clang headers (lib/include) with a link to
      libclang-common-22-dev; repack as ~us1 via Files-Excluded.
    - Generate a man page with help2man; run the upstream behaviour tests
      at build time and as autopkgtests.
    - Import debian/copyright and debian/lrc.config from Ubuntu.
  * debian/fetch-orig-source: download the upstream source tarball, verify
    its SHA-256 and minisign signature, and repack it with mk-origtargz.
  * debian/rules: fetch and unpack the upstream source automatically when
    building from a checkout that contains only debian/.
  * Add debian/update-upstream to move to the latest upstream release.
  * Provide /usr/bin/zig and zig(1) through update-alternatives, so the
    default can be chosen when several series are installed.
  * License the packaging under Expat, as Ubuntu's is; replace UNLICENSE
    with LICENSE and credit Ubuntu's authors in debian/copyright.
  * Point Vcs-* at github.com/danudey/zig-debian.

 -- Daniel Fox <danudey@me.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 09:26:32 -0700

zig (0.17.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, based on upstream's amd64 and arm64 binaries:

    <https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-x86_64-linux-0.17.0.tar.xz>
    <https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-aarch64-linux-0.17.0.tar.xz>

  * Add debian/fetch-orig-source, which verifies the upstream SHA-256 and
    minisign signature before repacking the orig tarball.
  * Install to /usr/lib/zig without a version-specific path, so new upstream
    releases only need a changelog entry.
  * Refuse to build when the orig tarball's binary does not match the host
    architecture; smoke-test the compiler during the build.
  * Do not strip or dwz the upstream binary.
  * Switch to debhelper compat 13; Standards-Version 4.7.3;
    Rules-Requires-Root: no.
  * Point Vcs-* at the packaging repository, and upstream links at Codeberg.
  * Update the watch file to version 4 and upstream's index.json.
  * Refresh lintian overrides for current lintian and upstream layout.
  * Rewrite debian/copyright to cover the third-party code bundled in lib/
    and statically linked into the compiler.
  * New maintainer.

 -- Daniel Fox <danudey@me.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:06:16 -0700

